  "output": "## Test Coverage Analysis — JARVIS Automation Scripts\n\n**Scope note:** This vault is primarily Obsidian markdown, not application code. The only testable logic lives in `70 Sistema/Automacao/morning-brief/` + `executive-assistant/dashboard.mjs`, plus two standalone scripts (`sample/scripts/external_id.js`, `scripts/bootstrap_jarvis_os.js`). None of these have a test runner, `package.json`, or a single test file — **current coverage is 0%**. I'm scoping the analysis to that real code (skipping `.obsidian/plugins/*/main.js`, which is vendored third-party code, and worktree duplicates under `.claude/worktrees/`).\n\nRecommendation: adopt Node's built-in `node:test` (zero dependencies, works natively with `.mjs`, available since Node 18) rather than pulling in Jest/Vitest for a handful of small files.\n\n---\n\n### 1. `lib/priority.mjs` — pure functions, highest test ROI, zero I/O\n\n| Function | Untested edge cases |\n|---|---|\n| `urgencyScore` | `prazo` null/undefined → 0; boundary equality at exactly `today`, `+3d`, `+7d`, `+30d` (uses `<=`, so off-by-one bugs are easy to introduce silently); date > 30 days out → 0 |\n| `energyBonus` | unknown/undefined value falls through to `0` — not just `\"alta\"` |\n| `projectScore` | `importancia: 0` / `valor_estrategico: 0` — `??` only defaults `null`/`undefined`, so `0` must NOT become `1` (easy regression if someone \"fixes\" it to `\\|\\|`) |\n| `isBlocked` | `status: \"pausado\"` short-circuits true even with no `dependencia`; `dependencia: []` (empty array) must be `false`, not truthy-array bug |\n| `toDate` | malformed string (e.g. `\"abc\"`) silently produces an `Invalid Date` instead of `null` — no validation at all |\n| `formatDateBR` | consequence of above: invalid date input renders `\"NaN/NaN\"` instead of `\"\"` |\n| `addDays` | year/month rollover (Dec 31 + 1), negative `n` |\n| `taskPriorityValue` | `rawLine` undefined; multiple priority emoji on one line (must take max, not first/last) |\n| `compareTasks` | tie-break when priorities equal; missing `due` must sort last (`\"9999\"` sentinel) |\n\n**Missing error handling test:** `toDate`/`formatDateBR` have no guard against garbage input — this should either be asserted as documented behavior or fixed and then tested.\n\n```js\n// 70 Sistema/Automacao/morning-brief/lib/__tests__/priority.test.mjs\nimport { test } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport {\n  urgencyScore, energyBonus, projectScore, isBlocked,\n  toDate, addDays, formatDateBR, taskPriorityValue, compareTasks,\n} from \"../priority.mjs\";\n\ntest(\"urgencyScore: boundary equality at exactly +3/+7/+30 days\", () => {\n  assert.equal(urgencyScore(\"2026-07-09\", \"2026-07-06\"), 8);  // +3d\n  assert.equal(urgencyScore(\"2026-07-13\", \"2026-07-06\"), 5);  // +7d\n  assert.equal(urgencyScore(\"2026-08-05\", \"2026-07-06\"), 2);  // +30d\n  assert.equal(urgencyScore(\"2026-08-06\", \"2026-07-06\"), 0);  // +31d\n});\n\ntest(\"urgencyScore: null/past prazo\", () => {\n  assert.equal(urgencyScore(null, \"2026-07-06\"), 0);\n  assert.equal(urgencyScore(\"2026-07-01\", \"2026-07-06\"), 12); // overdue\n});\n\ntest(\"projectScore: respects explicit 0, does not default to 1\", () => {\n  const note = { importancia: 0, valor_estrategico: 0 };\n  assert.equal(projectScore(note, \"2026-07-06\"), 0);\n});\n\ntest(\"isBlocked: empty dependencia array is NOT blocked\", () => {\n  assert.equal(isBlocked({ status: \"ativo\", dependencia: [] }), false);\n});\n\ntest(\"isBlocked: status pausado blocks regardless of dependencia\", () => {\n  assert.equal(isBlocked({ status: \"pausado\" }), true);\n});\n\ntest(\"toDate: invalid string does not throw (documents current behavior)\", () => {\n  const d = toDate(\"not-a-date\");\n  assert.equal(Number.isNaN(d.getTime()), true); // TODO: should this be null instead?\n});\n\ntest(\"formatDateBR: null returns empty string\", () => {\n  assert.equal(formatDateBR(null), \"\");\n});\n\ntest(\"addDays: crosses year boundary\", () => {\n  const d = addDays(new Date(2026, 11, 31), 1);\n  assert.equal(d.getFullYear(), 2027);\n  assert.equal(d.getMonth(), 0);\n  assert.equal(d.getDate(), 1);\n});\n\ntest(\"taskPriorityValue: takes max of multiple priority markers\", () => {\n  assert.equal(taskPriorityValue({ rawLine: \"- [ ] x 🔼 y ⏫ z\" }), 3);\n});\n\ntest(\"compareTasks: missing due sorts last\", () => {\n  const a = { rawLine: \"\", due: \"2026-07-10\" };\n  const b = { rawLine: \"\", due: null };\n  assert.ok(compareTasks(a, b) < 0);\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. `lib/vault.mjs` — filesystem parsing, currently the riskiest untested surface\n\nThe header comment even documents a **prior production bug** (CRLF files silently parsed as \"no tipo\") — that fix has zero regression coverage today.\n\n| Area | Untested edge cases |\n|---|---|\n| `walkMd` / `SKIP_FOLDERS` | `.obsidian`, `.claude`, `90 Arquivo`, `70 Sistema/Templates` must be skipped, including nested paths |\n| CRLF normalization | **regression test for the documented historical bug** — a CRLF-encoded note must still parse `tipo:` correctly |\n| `parseFrontmatter` | no `---` delimiter at all; unterminated frontmatter (no closing `---`) |\n| `parseSimpleYaml` | inline array `[a, b, c]`; multi-line list; quoted strings; boolean/number coercion; a bare `#` comment line |\n| `extractTasks` | task lines inside fenced code blocks must be ignored; 📅/⏳/✅ date extraction; malformed date (wrong format) leaves `due: null`; `cleanTaskText` stripping wikilinks/tags/priority emoji |\n| `isRecurringStale` | no `🔁` marker → false; `🔁` with no `due` → **stale (true)** by default; `🔁` with future `due` → false |\n| `loadVault` on a missing/unreadable directory | **finding, not just a gap:** `walkMd`'s `try { readdirSync } catch { return }` swallows the error silently, so `loadVault` never actually throws on a bad path — but `generate.mjs`/`dashboard.mjs` both wrap it in `try/catch` expecting a throw for the \"vault inacessível\" exit-1 path. That error path is currently **untestable/unreachable** via a missing directory. Worth a test that documents (and would catch a regression in either direction).\n\n```js\n// 70 Sistema/Automacao/morning-brief/lib/__tests__/vault.test.mjs\nimport { test } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport os from \"node:os\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { loadVault, extractTasks, isRecurringStale } from \"../vault.mjs\";\n\nfunction makeTempVault(files) {\n  const dir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"jarvis-vault-\"));\n  for (const [rel, content] of Object.entries(files)) {\n    const full = path.join(dir, rel);\n    fs.mkdirSync(path.dirname(full), { recursive: true });\n    fs.writeFileSync(full, content);\n  }\n  return dir;\n}\n\ntest(\"loadVault: CRLF-encoded frontmatter still parses tipo (regression)\", () => {\n  const dir = makeTempVault({\n    \"nota.md\": \"---\\r\\ntipo: projeto\\r\\nstatus: ativo\\r\\n---\\r\\nCorpo\\r\\n\",\n  });\n  const { notes } = loadVault(dir);\n  assert.equal(notes[0].tipo, \"projeto\");\n});\n\ntest(\"loadVault: skips .obsidian, .claude, 90 Arquivo, Templates\", () => {\n  const dir = makeTempVault({\n    \".obsidian/plugin.md\": \"---\\ntipo: x\\n---\\n\",\n    \"90 Arquivo/old.md\": \"---\\ntipo: x\\n---\\n\",\n    \"70 Sistema/Templates/t.md\": \"---\\ntipo: x\\n---\\n\",\n    \"20 Pessoal/real.md\": \"---\\ntipo: projeto\\n---\\n\",\n  });\n  const { notes } = loadVault(dir);\n  assert.equal(notes.length, 1);\n  assert.equal(notes[0].basename, \"real\");\n});\n\ntest(\"loadVault: on missing directory, returns empty (documents current silent-swallow behavior)\", () => {\n  const result = loadVault(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"does-not-exist-xyz\"));\n  assert.deepEqual(result, { notes: [], tasks: [] });\n  // NOTE: generate.mjs's try/catch around loadVault assumes a throw is possible —\n  // confirm that assumption still holds if vault.mjs's error handling ever changes.\n});\n\ntest(\"extractTasks: ignores task-like lines inside fenced code blocks\", () => {\n  const body = \"```\\n- [ ] not a real task\\n```\\n- [ ] real task 📅 2026-07-10\";\n  const tasks = extractTasks(body, { path: \"n.md\", basename: \"n\" });\n  assert.equal(tasks.length, 1);\n  assert.equal(tasks[0].due, \"2026-07-10\");\n});\n\ntest(\"extractTasks: cleanTaskText strips wikilinks, tags, priority emoji\", () => {\n  const body = \"- [ ] 🔼 falar com [[Cliente X]] #urgente\";\n  const tasks = extractTasks(body, { path: \"n.md\", basename: \"n\" });\n  assert.equal(tasks[0].text, \"falar com Cliente X\");\n});\n\ntest(\"isRecurringStale: recurring task with no due date is stale\", () => {\n  assert.equal(isRecurringStale({ rawLine: \"- [ ] x 🔁 every day\" }, \"2026-07-06\"), true);\n});\n\ntest(\"isRecurringStale: non-recurring task is never stale\", () => {\n  assert.equal(isRecurringStale({ rawLine: \"- [ ] x\", due: \"2020-01-01\" }, \"2026-07-06\"), false);\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. `lib/brief.mjs` — core business logic, entirely untested\n\nThis is the highest-value file to cover since it drives both the Morning Brief and the Daily Dashboard.\n\n| Function (internal, exercised via `buildMorningBrief`) | Untested edge cases |\n|---|---|\n| `selectTop3` | recurring-stale tasks excluded; today-due tasks ranked before overdue; `done: true` excluded; slice-to-3 |\n| `collectRisks` | `tipo` filter (only `projeto`/`objetivo`); `status` exclusion list (`concluido`/`arquivado`/`abandonado`); `ProjectAtRisk` boundary (`daysLeft` 0–3 inclusive, `progresso < 70` exclusive); overdue tasks exclude `habito` tipo and `/Habitos/` path; overdue slice-to-5; **dedup across risk sources** |\n| `collectCommercial` | `lead` status; 7-day horizon boundary for `proximo_contato`; overdue follow-up → `RevenueRiskDetected` vs future → `MeetingScheduled`; high-value pipeline (`valor >= 10000`) within 3 days can **double-emit** with the follow-up check — needs a test asserting dedup actually collapses it |\n| `selectProjectsAttention` | excludes blocked projects; sorts by score descending; slice-to-3 |\n| `collectToday` | meeting title strips leading date prefix; `cliente` meta strips brackets/quotes; case-insensitive dedup of same-text tasks from `due` vs `scheduled` |\n| `formatBriefText` | all five empty-state strings (no tests currently assert the \"nothing to show\" copy) |\n| `formatDependency`/`stripLink` | array of wikilinks vs single string vs plain text |\n\n```js\n// 70 Sistema/Automacao/morning-brief/lib/__tests__/brief.test.mjs\nimport { test } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport { buildMorningBrief } from \"../brief.mjs\";\n\nconst TODAY = \"2026-07-06\";\n\ntest(\"buildMorningBrief: empty vault produces all empty-state sections\", () => {\n  const brief = buildMorningBrief({ notes: [], tasks: [] }, { today: TODAY });\n  assert.equal(brief.top3.length, 0);\n  assert.match(brief.text, /nenhuma ação crítica para hoje/);\n  assert.match(brief.text, /nada travado/);\n});\n\ntest(\"collectRisks: excludes concluido/arquivado/abandonado projects\", () => {\n  const notes = [\n    { tipo: \"projeto\", status: \"concluido\", dependencia: [\"x\"] },\n  ];\n  const brief = buildMorningBrief({ notes, tasks: [] }, { today: TODAY });\n  assert.equal(brief.risks.length, 0);\n});\n\ntest(\"collectRisks: ProjectAtRisk boundary — daysLeft=3 & progresso=69 fires, progresso=70 does not\", () => {\n  const base = { tipo: \"projeto\", status: \"ativo\", prazo: \"2026-07-09\", basename: \"P\" };\n  const risky = buildMorningBrief({ notes: [{ ...base, progresso: 69 }], tasks: [] }, { today: TODAY });\n  const safe = buildMorningBrief({ notes: [{ ...base, progresso: 70 }], tasks: [] }, { today: TODAY });\n  assert.ok(risky.risks.some((r) => r.kind === \"ProjectAtRisk\"));\n  assert.ok(!safe.risks.some((r) => r.kind === \"ProjectAtRisk\"));\n});\n\ntest(\"collectRisks: overdue habit tasks are excluded from MissedDeadline\", () => {\n  const tasks = [\n    { done: false, due: \"2026-07-01\", text: \"treino\", sourceTipo: \"habito\", sourcePath: \"20 Pessoal/Habitos/x.md\", rawLine: \"\" },\n  ];\n  const brief = buildMorningBrief({ notes: [], tasks }, { today: TODAY });\n  assert.equal(brief.risks.length, 0);\n});\n\ntest(\"collectCommercial: high-value pipeline + overdue follow-up dedupes to one item\", () => {\n  const notes = [{\n    tipo: \"cliente\", status: \"ativo\", basename: \"Cliente Y\",\n    valor: 15000, proximo_contato: \"2026-07-05\",\n  }];\n  const brief = buildMorningBrief({ notes, tasks: [] }, { today: TODAY });\n  const texts = brief.commercial.map((c) => c.text);\n  assert.equal(new Set(texts).size, texts.length); // no duplicate text entries\n});\n\ntest(\"collectToday: strips date prefix from meeting title and formats cliente meta\", () => {\n  const notes = [{ tipo: \"reuniao\", data: TODAY, basename: \"2026-07-06 Kickoff\", cliente: '\"[[Acme]]\"' }];\n  const brief = buildMorningBrief({ notes, tasks: [] }, { today: TODAY });\n  assert.equal(brief.today[0].text, \"Kickoff\");\n  assert.equal(brief.today[0].meta, \"Acme\");\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. `lib/slack.mjs` — network I/O, zero coverage of failure modes\n\n| Function | Untested edge cases |\n|---|---|\n| `publishToSlack` | precedence order (n8n > webhook > bot token); no delivery method configured → must throw the specific config error |\n| `postN8nWebhook` | `dryRun` skips `fetch` entirely; non-2xx response → error includes status + body; JSON-parse failure on a 2xx response falls back to raw text instead of crashing |\n| `postSlackIncomingWebhook` | dryRun; non-2xx throws |\n| `postBotMessage` | dryRun; `data.ok === false` throws using `data.error`, falls back to `\"unknown\"` |\n| `loadPostState` | missing file → `null`; **corrupt JSON → `null`, not a crash** (currently untested `catch`) |\n| `alreadyPostedToday` | `force: true` always bypasses; date mismatch; `posted: false` on matching date |\n\n**Missing error handling test:** none of the three delivery paths' error branches are exercised — a fetch that throws (network down) isn't caught anywhere in `slack.mjs`, meaning it propagates to `generate.mjs`'s catch — worth an explicit test that this propagation happens as intended.\n\n```js\n// 70 Sistema/Automacao/morning-brief/lib/__tests__/slack.test.mjs\nimport { test, beforeEach, afterEach } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport os from \"node:os\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport {\n  publishToSlack, loadPostState, savePostState, alreadyPostedToday,\n} from \"../slack.mjs\";\n\nlet originalFetch;\nbeforeEach(() => { originalFetch = globalThis.fetch; });\nafterEach(() => { globalThis.fetch = originalFetch; });\n\ntest(\"publishToSlack: throws when no delivery method configured\", async () => {\n  await assert.rejects(() => publishToSlack(\"text\", {}, {}));\n});\n\ntest(\"publishToSlack: n8nWebhookUrl takes precedence over slackWebhookUrl\", async () => {\n  let calledUrl = null;\n  globalThis.fetch = async (url) => { calledUrl = url; return { ok: true, json: async () => ({}) }; };\n  await publishToSlack(\"text\", { n8nWebhookUrl: \"https://n8n\", slackWebhookUrl: \"https://slack\" }, {});\n  assert.equal(calledUrl, \"https://n8n\");\n});\n\ntest(\"publishToSlack: dryRun never calls fetch\", async () => {\n  globalThis.fetch = async () => { throw new Error(\"should not be called\"); };\n  const result = await publishToSlack(\"text\", { n8nWebhookUrl: \"https://n8n\" }, { dryRun: true });\n  assert.equal(result.dryRun, true);\n});\n\ntest(\"publishToSlack: n8n non-2xx response throws with status and body\", async () => {\n  globalThis.fetch = async () => ({ ok: false, status: 500, text: async () => \"boom\" });\n  await assert.rejects(\n    () => publishToSlack(\"text\", { n8nWebhookUrl: \"https://n8n\" }, {}),\n    /500/\n  );\n});\n\ntest(\"publishToSlack: bot API ok:false throws with data.error\", async () => {\n  globalThis.fetch = async () => ({ ok: true, json: async () => ({ ok: false, error: \"invalid_auth\" }) });\n  await assert.rejects(\n    () => publishToSlack(\"text\", { slackBotToken: \"t\", slackChannel: \"#c\" }, {}),\n    /invalid_auth/\n  );\n});\n\ntest(\"loadPostState: corrupt JSON returns null instead of throwing\", () => {\n  const dir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"state-\"));\n  const file = path.join(dir, \"state.json\");\n  fs.writeFileSync(file, \"{not json\");\n  assert.equal(loadPostState(file), null);\n});\n\ntest(\"alreadyPostedToday: force=true always bypasses\", () => {\n  assert.equal(alreadyPostedToday({ date: \"2026-07-06\", posted: true }, \"2026-07-06\", true), false);\n});\n\ntest(\"alreadyPostedToday: date mismatch returns false even if posted\", () => {\n  assert.equal(alreadyPostedToday({ date: \"2026-07-05\", posted: true }, \"2026-07-06\", false), false);\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Integration gaps (`generate.mjs`, `dashboard.mjs`)\n\nBoth files are CLI entrypoints that call `main()` unconditionally at import time — there's no `if (import.meta.url === ...)` guard. That's a structural gap: **you cannot `import` these modules in a test without triggering a real run** (file writes, possible network call). Two options, in order of preference:\n\n1. Refactor to export `main()` and guard the auto-invoke, enabling in-process integration tests.\n2. Until then, test them as black-box subprocesses via `child_process.execFileSync` against a temp vault + `JARVIS_VAULT_ROOT` env var (already supported by `dashboard.mjs`; `generate.mjs` would need the same env override added to `loadConfig`, which today only reads `config.json` or hardcoded relative paths).\n\n**Missing error handling found:** `generate.mjs`'s `loadConfig()` calls `JSON.parse` on `config.json` with no `try/catch` — a malformed config file crashes the whole run before any logging happens. This should be tested and probably wrapped.\n\n```js\n// 70 Sistema/Automacao/executive-assistant/__tests__/dashboard.integration.test.mjs\nimport { test } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport { execFileSync } from \"node:child_process\";\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport os from \"node:os\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\n\nfunction makeTempVault() {\n  const dir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"jarvis-dash-\"));\n  fs.mkdirSync(path.join(dir, \"raw\"), { recursive: true });\n  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dir, \"raw\", \"inbox.md\"), \"## Capturas pendentes\\n- item 1\\n- item 2\\n\");\n  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dir, \"projeto.md\"), \"---\\ntipo: projeto\\nstatus: ativo\\nprazo: 2026-07-08\\nprogresso: 40\\n---\\n\");\n  return dir;\n}\n\ntest(\"dashboard.mjs: --dry-run does not write output file, reflects inbox count\", () => {\n  const vault = makeTempVault();\n  const scriptPath = path.resolve(\"70 Sistema/Automacao/executive-assistant/dashboard.mjs\");\n  const out = execFileSync(\"node\", [scriptPath, \"--dry-run\", \"--print\"], {\n    env: { ...process.env, JARVIS_VAULT_ROOT: vault },\n    encoding: \"utf8\",\n  });\n  assert.match(out, /2.*capturas aguardam triagem/);\n  assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(vault, \"output\", \"daily_dashboard.md\")), false);\n});\n\ntest(\"dashboard.mjs: normal run writes output/daily_dashboard.md\", () => {\n  const vault = makeTempVault();\n  const scriptPath = path.resolve(\"70 Sistema/Automacao/executive-assistant/dashboard.mjs\");\n  execFileSync(\"node\", [scriptPath], { env: { ...process.env, JARVIS_VAULT_ROOT: vault } });\n  const written = fs.readFileSync(path.join(vault, \"output\", \"daily_dashboard.md\"), \"utf8\");\n  assert.match(written, /# Daily Dashboard/);\n});\n```\n\nFor `generate.mjs`, the same pattern applies but first requires adding a `JARVIS_VAULT_ROOT`-style override to `loadConfig()` (currently vault root is derived only from `__dirname` or `config.json`) — flagging that as a prerequisite rather than writing a skeleton that can't actually run yet.\n\n---\n\n### 6. `sample/scripts/external_id.js` — small pure function, easy win\n\n```js\n// sample/scripts/__tests__/external_id.test.js\nconst { test } = require(\"node:test\");\nconst assert = require(\"node:assert/strict\");\nconst { generateExternalId } = require(\"../external_id.js\");\n\ntest(\"generateExternalId: returns 12-char hex string\", () => {\n  const id = generateExternalId(\"/repo\", \"notes/a.md\");\n  assert.match(id, /^[a-f0-9]{12}$/);\n});\n\ntest(\"generateExternalId: deterministic for same inputs\", () => {\n  assert.equal(\n    generateExternalId(\"/repo\", \"notes/a.md\"),\n    generateExternalId(\"/repo\", \"notes/a.md\")\n  );\n});\n\ntest(\"generateExternalId: different notePath yields different id\", () => {\n  assert.notEqual(\n    generateExternalId(\"/repo\", \"notes/a.md\"),\n    generateExternalId(\"/repo\", \"notes/b.md\")\n  );\n});\n\ntest(\"generateExternalId: trailing slash in repoRoot normalizes to same id\", () => {\n  assert.equal(\n    generateExternalId(\"/repo\", \"notes/a.md\"),\n    generateExternalId(\"/repo/\", \"notes/a.md\")\n  );\n});\n```\n\n`scripts/bootstrap_jarvis_os.js` is a one-shot idempotent scaffolder (not part of any runtime path) — low priority; if you want coverage, the only thing worth asserting is that re-running it doesn't overwrite/duplicate existing chapter files, but I'd deprioritize this relative to the Morning Brief/Dashboard logic above.\n\n---\n\n### Summary of gaps by severity\n\n1. **No test infrastructure exists at all** — recommend `node --test` + a `package.json` with `\"scripts\": {\"test\": \"node --test '70 Sistema/**/*.test.mjs' 'sample/**/*.test.js'\"}`.\n2. **`vault.mjs` has zero regression coverage for a documented past production bug** (CRLF parsing) — highest priority to close first.\n3. **`generate.mjs`/`dashboard.mjs` main() auto-invokes on import** — blocks in-process testing; needs a guard refactor before real integration tests are practical.\n4. **Unhandled malformed `config.json`** in `generate.mjs` crashes before any logging.\n5. **`toDate`/`formatDateBR` have no input validation** — garbage input produces `Invalid Date` / `\"NaN/NaN\"` silently.\n6. **Slack delivery failure paths are completely untested** — no test proves n8n/webhook/bot-token error messages actually surface correctly to the operator.\n\nWant me to actually create these test files and wire up `package.json` + `node --test`, or keep this as an analysis-only deliverable for now?\n",
